# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PinPoint environment variables
#
#   cp .env.example .env      (never commit .env — it is git-ignored)
#
# Vite restarts the dev server automatically when .env changes; if the values
# still do not show up, stop and start `npm run dev` again. On Vercel, add the
# same variables under Project → Settings → Environment Variables and REDEPLOY
# (variables added after a build only apply to the next deployment).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Firebase (client SDK config — these values are public by design) ─────────
# Firebase Console → Project settings (gear) → General → "Your apps" → Web app
# → SDK setup and configuration → Config.  All six values are required for
# Google sign-in to work.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSy...
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project-id.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project-id.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=123456789012
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:123456789012:web:abcdef1234567890

# Aliases also work if your project already uses them (vite.config.js resolves
# them into the bundle): FIREBASE_API_KEY, REACT_APP_FIREBASE_API_KEY,
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY, … and the same for the other five fields.

# ── Two console switches that are NOT in the .env file ──────────────────────
# 1) Enable the provider:  Authentication → Sign-in method → Google → Enable.
# 2) Allow your domain:    Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains →
#    Add domain:  localhost · your-app.vercel.app · any preview domain you use.
#    Sign-in from a domain that is not listed fails with
#    "auth/unauthorized-domain" — the app now shows that message in the modal.

# ── EdgeStore (image uploads; optional — falls back to local compression) ───
# https://edgestore.dev → create a project → copy the access/secret keys.
EDGE_STORE_ACCESS_KEY=
EDGE_STORE_SECRET_KEY=
